RATIONALE: The claim manufactures a failure by asserting a "production baseline" sliding window of W=16. Production safety models and blocklists require significantly larger contexts to evaluate semantics, and retaining 128–256 tokens in a string buffer adds zero meaningful overhead. Because any realistic safety team would configure a window far larger than the runtime's chunk size (W >> C), the cross-org seam vulnerability does not exist in practice.
